en-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Erim</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Hand Dominance and motor unit firing behaviour.</article-title><source>J Neurophys</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>1373</fpage><lpage>1382</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001748-Thomas1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>ALR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>The aerodynamic costs of asymmetry in the wings and tails of birds: asymmetric birds can't fly round tight corners.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc B</source><volume>254</volume><fpage>181</fpage><lpage>189</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001748-Mller1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000f8;ller</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Swaddle</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Asymmetry, developmental stability and evolution.</article-title><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001748-Swaddle1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Swaddle</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Witter</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The effects of molt on the flight performance, body mass and behaviour of European Starlings (<italic>Sturnus vulgaris</italic>).</article-title><source>Can J Zool</source><volume>75</volume><fpage>948</fpage><lpage>953</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001748-Mller2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000f8;ller</surname><given-names>AP</given-nam